# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase core, story MOCK3-2.

LOCATED FIX SITE(S) — traced in this repository before you were asked. Anchor every criterion to the behaviour THIS code produces:
- src/schedule.ts :: formatStops — The for-loop bound `i < stops.length - 1` excludes the last index, so the final stop is never pushed into parts. Changing the bound to `i < stops.length` makes every stop, including the last, appear in the rendered string. The separator `' -> '` already exists on line 9 and is reused unchanged.
- test/schedule.test.ts :: schedule.test.ts — Existing tests only assert that the output contains '->' and 'Union'; none check the last stop ('Eglinton'). Once formatStops is fixed, a test must verify the final stop name appears in the rendered string, and that an empty line still renders without error (matching the acceptance criteria).


DECLARED FILES — the actual contents of the files this story names or the detective located. Base every observable criterion on what THIS code does, not on what the title suggests:
--- src/schedule.ts
/** Renders a stop sequence for a departure board. */
export type Stop = { name: string; minutes: number };

export function formatStops(stops: Stop[]): string {
  const parts: string[] = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < stops.length - 1; i++) {
    parts.push(`${stops[i].name} (${stops[i].minutes}m)`);
  }
  return parts.join(' -> ');
}

export function totalMinutes(stops: Stop[]): number {
  return stops.length ? stops[stops.length - 1].minutes : 0;
}

--- test/schedule.test.ts
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { formatStops, totalMinutes } from '../src/schedule';

const LINE = [
  { name: 'Union', minutes: 0 },
  { name: 'Bloor', minutes: 12 },
  { name: 'Eglinton', minutes: 25 },
];

describe('formatStops', () => {
  it('separates stops with an arrow', () => {
    expect(formatStops(LINE)).toContain('->');
  });
  it('names the first stop', () => {
    expect(formatStops(LINE)).toContain('Union');
  });
});

describe('totalMinutes', () => {
  it('reports the journey length', () => { expect(totalMinutes(LINE)).toBe(25); });
  it('handles an empty line', () => { expect(totalMinutes([])).toBe(0); });
});



